WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.589 --> 00:00:02.744
(lively music)

00:00:02.744 --> 00:00:04.244
- Musical spaces are gendered.

00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:08.440
The history of choral
singing is that women sing

00:00:08.440 --> 00:00:12.790
in high voices, and men
sing in their lower voices,

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:16.470
and for an individual for
whom that model does not fit,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.903
choir is not really a space for them.

00:00:22.157 --> 00:00:24.690
I'm really trying to
create a new tradition

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:27.773
and create spaces for trans
and non-binary singers.

00:00:30.808 --> 00:00:32.050
- [Announcer] This Great
Big Story was made possible

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:33.083
by Proctor &amp; Gamble.

00:00:34.506 --> 00:00:37.256
(choral singing)

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:43.440
I'm William Sauerland, and
I'm the artistic director

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.613
of the Oakland Gay Men's Chorus.

00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:51.170
I'm trying to make a new model

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:54.470
for what a men's chorus can look like.

00:00:55.768 --> 00:00:57.070
We've performed at the professional level

00:00:57.070 --> 00:01:00.100
in big concert halls in
front of two thousand people,

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:02.640
all the way down to small church venues

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:05.530
with maybe 50 or 60 audience members.

00:01:05.530 --> 00:01:09.960
The chorus is made up of
gay men, bi men, trans men,

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:14.330
non-binary individuals,
straight men, cisgender women.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:17.636
Everyone is allowed to
have a place at the table.

00:01:17.636 --> 00:01:21.603
Let's do that again; let's
do that the whole page.

00:01:21.603 --> 00:01:26.603
(choral singing)
(piano playing)

00:01:30.027 --> 00:01:33.510
I wouldn't characterize having
trans or non-binary singers

00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:35.533
in a chorus as a challenge.

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.300
If you have a trans
singer who's going through

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:42.750
a vocal change, it might
mean allowing them to move

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:45.510
the vocal parts as their voice deepens

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:46.783
or changes in some way.

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:54.040
I want anybody who feels like
their voice has been silenced

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:56.503
to make their voice even louder.

00:01:57.910 --> 00:02:00.660
(choral singing)

00:02:04.614 --> 00:02:08.114
(sewing machine whirring)

00:02:09.288 --> 00:02:11.955
(light singing)

00:02:17.929 --> 00:02:18.983
- I have always loved singing.

00:02:20.054 --> 00:02:23.830
I sang with the symphony, but
I was in the alto section,

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:26.170
and I really wanted to be
in the section behind me.

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:28.060
They got to wear tuxes.

00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.160
I had to wear a dress.

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.520
When I decided to transition,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:35.260
I found that there were
places that didn't want me.

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:38.163
I felt like I had to
apologize for who I was.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:43.380
When I joined the
chorus, I had been afraid

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:45.970
because I thought my
voice stood out too much.

00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.903
It's like it's not masculine enough.

00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:52.720
I felt so self-conscious
'cause my voice is different;

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.120
it's different from theirs.

00:02:55.120 --> 00:02:57.060
I want my voice to be like theirs,

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.163
but, you know, that's a hard journey.

00:03:01.662 --> 00:03:03.409
♪ Some days ♪

00:03:03.409 --> 00:03:05.040
♪ It seems like ♪

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:07.610
♪ Love's in short supply ♪

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:10.460
Once I got in there and
started making friends,

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:14.050
I felt like I had walked into
a family of so many brothers.

00:03:14.050 --> 00:03:16.870
I'd take my kid, Al, to rehearsals,

00:03:16.870 --> 00:03:19.393
and Al had a whole bunch of uncles.

00:03:20.537 --> 00:03:21.780
♪ So starting ♪

00:03:21.780 --> 00:03:25.820
Suddenly, I was in a place where
I could start just being me

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:29.593
and they let me be comfortable.

00:03:31.747 --> 00:03:33.777
- Ready, and a...

00:03:33.777 --> 00:03:36.527
(choral singing)

00:03:42.257 --> 00:03:44.930
- In one of the shows,
I got to sing the solo.

00:03:44.930 --> 00:03:48.320
When I was done, Billy blew me a kiss,

00:03:48.320 --> 00:03:53.320
and in that moment, I knew my
voice as David was accepted.

00:03:55.990 --> 00:03:57.723
It was OK for me to be me.

00:03:58.831 --> 00:04:01.581
(choral singing)

00:04:04.057 --> 00:04:06.640
(bright music)

00:04:07.896 --> 00:04:10.490
- We are not taking any
step back by having trans

00:04:10.490 --> 00:04:12.344
and non-binary singers.

00:04:12.344 --> 00:04:13.400
Our sound has not suffered.

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.453
In fact, it's the opposite.

00:04:17.357 --> 00:04:20.070
We actually sound better
because of these singers.

00:04:20.070 --> 00:04:23.620
Our community and our sense
of family is even stronger

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.890
because we have said in an outward way

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:30.320
that you are all welcome,
and music is the thing

00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:31.593
that brings us together.

00:04:32.925 --> 00:04:35.508
(lively music)

